  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This software record shows early but tangible uptake: 56 downloads, 178 views, and one documented downstream reuse in a biomedical article. The broader citation record is still at zero, so the evidence points to initial use and discoverability rather than established scholarly accumulation.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Zenodo-hosted software release is associated with a published PLOS Biology paper and is openly accessible through a recognized repository infrastructure. The strongest evidence of impact in the current record is usage: the item has been viewed 178 times and downloaded 56 times, indicating that readers are finding and accessing the software.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">There is also one documented downstream reuse, captured as a biomedical article mention in Europe PMC. That signal suggests the software has already been incorporated into the surrounding research literature, even though the citation count in OpenAlex remains at zero. In other words, the record shows early scholarly attention and reuse, but not yet a citation trail.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The stewardship signals are also solid. The software is deposited in Zenodo, with an open access record and a linked published version on GitHub, which supports transparency, reproducibility, and long-term access. This kind of repository-backed distribution is especially important for software because it makes the release easier for others to inspect, reuse, and extend.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the impact story here is one of modest but meaningful early reach: the software is being accessed, it has at least one documented reuse in the biomedical literature, and it is being maintained in a trusted repository environment. The record is still too sparse to support stronger claims about field-level influence, but it does show the beginnings of practical and scholarly adoption.</p>",
